// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`formatDecision > AUDIT_UNAVAILABLE: names its code, is plain, short and stable 1`] = `
"engagement-guard: DENIED [AUDIT_UNAVAILABLE]: the audit log cannot be written, so network actions fail closed
Target: 192.0.2.10: in-scope, rule in[0]: 192.0.2.0/24
Detail: ENOSPC: no space left on device
Tier: recon
Case: acme-ext-2026 (.guard/engagement.yaml)
The operator must restore the audit log (disk space, permissions), then check it with \`engagement-guard audit verify\`."
`;

exports[`formatDecision > BLACKOUT: names its code, is plain, short and stable 1`] = `
"engagement-guard: DENIED [BLACKOUT]: inside a blackout period of the engagement
Target: 192.0.2.10: blackout, no matching scope rule
Rule: roe.blackout_hours[0]: Mon–Fri 12:00–13:00 Europe/London
Tier: recon
Case: acme-ext-2026 (.guard/engagement.yaml)
Nothing overrides blackout hours; only an audited \`engagement-guard engagement edit\` changes them. Do not try to work around this check."
`;

exports[`formatDecision > CASE_INVALID: names its code, is plain, short and stable 1`] = `
"engagement-guard: DENIED [CASE_INVALID]: the case file failed validation
Target: 192.0.2.10: no-engagement, no matching scope rule
Detail: scope.in[1]: expected an IP, range, hostname or URL
Tier: recon
Case: none active (expected at .guard/engagement.yaml)
The operator must fix the case file; \`engagement-guard engagement validate\` lists every error."
`;

exports[`formatDecision > EXPLOITATION_CONFIRM: names its code, is plain, short and stable 1`] = `
"engagement-guard: NEEDS CONFIRMATION (unskippable) [EXPLOITATION_CONFIRM]: exploitation is authorised by the RoE but needs the operator to confirm
Target: https://portal.acme.example/login: in-scope, rule in[3]: https://portal.acme.example/
Tier: exploitation
Case: acme-ext-2026 (.guard/engagement.yaml)
This confirmation can never be skipped, remembered or pre-approved."
`;

exports[`formatDecision > FIRST_RUN_REQUIRED: names its code, is plain, short and stable 1`] = `
"engagement-guard: DENIED [FIRST_RUN_REQUIRED]: security tools are locked until the first-run acknowledgement is completed
Target: 192.0.2.10: no-engagement, no matching scope rule
Tier: recon
Case: none active (expected at .guard/engagement.yaml)
The operator must complete the first-run acknowledgement (\`engagement-guard ack\`). Do not try to work around this check."
`;

exports[`formatDecision > GUARD_ERROR: names its code, is plain, short and stable 1`] = `
"engagement-guard: DENIED [GUARD_ERROR]: internal error in the scope guard; the action failed closed
Targets: none extracted
Detail: TypeError: cannot read properties of undefined
Case: acme-ext-2026 (.guard/engagement.yaml)
Tell the operator. Do not retry the action in another form."
`;

exports[`formatDecision > HARD_REFUSAL: names its code, is plain, short and stable 1`] = `
"engagement-guard: DENIED [HARD_REFUSAL]: refused: the action is on the hard denylist
Target: 192.0.2.10: in-scope, rule in[0]: 192.0.2.0/24
Rule: nmap-script-dos: nmap --script selecting DoS scripts or categories that include them
Suggestion: --script "vuln and not dos"
Case: acme-ext-2026 (.guard/engagement.yaml)
Hard refusals cannot be approved or allowed by any case, mode, grant or setting. Do not try to work around this check."
`;

exports[`formatDecision > IN_SCOPE: names its code, is plain, short and stable 1`] = `
"engagement-guard: PASS [IN_SCOPE]: all targets are in scope; tier and rate are within the RoE
Target: 192.0.2.10: in-scope, rule in[0]: 192.0.2.0/24
Tier: recon
Case: acme-ext-2026 (.guard/engagement.yaml)
Core permission rules decide next."
`;

exports[`formatDecision > INFRA_NOT_TARGET: names its code, is plain, short and stable 1`] = `
"engagement-guard: DENIED [INFRA_NOT_TARGET]: trusted infrastructure is not a target
Target: registry.npmjs.org (infrastructure): trusted-infra, rule trusted_infrastructure: registry.npmjs.org
Tier: vuln-scan
Case: acme-ext-2026 (.guard/engagement.yaml)
Registries, code hosts and resolvers may be fetched from, never scanned, fuzzed, brute-forced or exploited. Do not try to work around this check."
`;

